# System requirements

The `rawrr` executable will run out of the box.

I you want to build on your own follow the text below.

## Compile and Link yourself

In case you prefer to compile `rawrr.exe` from C# source code, please install
the .NET 8.0

### Linux (debian:10/ubuntu:20.04) (debian:12/ubuntu:24)

```{sh}
## DEPRECIATED: sudo apt-get install mono-mcs mono-xbuild
sudo apt-get install dotnet-sdk-8.0
```

### macOS (Catalina/BigSur/.../Sequoia)

<https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download>

### Microsoft Windows

<https://dotnet.microsoft.com/en-us/download>

## Install the .NET assemblies

assemblies aka Common Intermediate Language bytecode

In general, ThermoFisher.CommonCore dlls can be obtained through:

<https://github.com/thermofisherlsms/RawFileReader>

or

by contacting Jim Shofstahl using

<jim.Shofstahl@thermofisher.com>

## build

* source nuget pkgs

* add libraries

* (cross)-dcompile and link

You can use the provided `rawrrassembly/build.sh` script to automate publishing the `rawrr-dotnet.csproj` for multiple platforms. This script handles building and placing the assemblies in the appropriate cache directories for macOS, Windows, and Linux.

To use the script:

```sh
cd rawrrassembly
./build.sh
```

This will generate the platform-specific assemblies in:

* `/Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/osx-x64`
* `/Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/win-x64`
* `/Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/linux-x64`

Alternatively, you can manually publish using the following commands:

```sh
dotnet publish rawrr-dotnet.csproj --os osx -a x64 --output /Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/osx-x64
dotnet publish rawrr-dotnet.csproj --os win -a x64 --output /Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/win-x64
dotnet publish rawrr-dotnet.csproj --os linux -a x64 --output /Users/cp/Library/Caches/org.R-project.R/R/rawrr/rawrrassembly/linux-x64
```

To generate a single large (~110MB) binary for each platform:

```sh
dotnet publish -c Release -r linux-x64 -p PublishReadyToRun=true
dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64 -p PublishReadyToRun=true
dotnet publish -c Release -r osx-x64 -p PublishReadyToRun=true
```

## Docker

### Build the image

```sh
docker build -t rawrr:latest .
```

### Run interactively

```sh
docker run -it --rm -v $(pwd):/workspace rawrr:latest
```

### Build and check the package

```sh
docker run -it --rm -v $(pwd):/workspace rawrr:latest R CMD build .
docker run -it --rm -v $(pwd):/workspace rawrr:latest R CMD check rawrr_*.tar.gz
```

## Required packages to run `R CMD INSTALL`

```r
BiocManager::install('ExperimentHub')
BiocManager::install('tartare')
```
